I  remember like eating a salad or ordering  a Greek salad at like like ten weeks  pregnant or something and then just like  eating the feta cheese off the top and I  was like mmm that was a waste of money I  could have just had a block of cheese so  now that I am further along and I'm kind  of like past that I'm feeling good  I can eat vegetables again and it's so  exciting I guess if there's anything I'm  craving it's like really  you see water-rich things so like  vegetables and fruit like acidic fruits  like pineapple well when I was in  Florida I eat a ton of watermelon and  that was so exciting I eat a lot of  clementines so let a lot of those kind  of like tangy acidic foods are really  feeling good for me right now but I I  love hearing about people's cravings so  leafy comments below if if there was  something funny and weird that you were  craving I can't really think of anything  for myself I wish I did I wish I did  because it's just something fun to to  remember as part of your pregnancy but  nope I'm boring I just like I love  vegetables and fruit and other dietician  tea things so who knows okay do you have  any other ideas for morning sickness so  great question lots of ginger choose  anything kind of tangy like I said  acidic things tend to help and lemon  ginger tea was a lifesaver for me I  drank a lot of that and I just brewed it  myself so I just literally just like  steeped ginger in water and then added  lots of lemon juice and I love that and  if you can even add a little honey if  that's too acidic for you but I just  like the UH tang and so the other thing  I would say is just like kind of small  energy dense meals and snacks so I  really try to focus on not be like big  volumous meals so like where I might  have a salad normally the salad would  just be like too much for me I couldn't  like get through it so I really focused  on adding more fats to my meals just to  add more calories in there so like not  better like cooking with a little bit  more fat avocado sprinkling hemp parts  or chia seeds or or or flax on basically  everything these little nutritional  boosters do add up throughout the day  without making you feel overly full or  uncomfortable as for carbs I had no  guilt about eating like mainly carbs in  the first trimester I just tried  whenever possible to choose kind of like  a slow digesting carb carb that had a  little bit of protein in it or paired  with some  protein so for example like whole-grain  bread with maybe some fat or protein  some like nut butter or some avocado or  like the avocado toast that I showed you  in my video which I'll link to below I  also did like oatmeal with lots of hemp  arts or nut butter swirled in loved that  I had like oatmeal for breakfast and  lunch and dinner somedays no no guilt no  shame what else Oh  bean based pasta is amazing I use it a  lot of my recipes but and I love it for  my kid as well because you know picky  toddlers and morning sick  pregnant ladies are not that different  when it comes to their diet so bean  based pasta is great because at least if  like I just felt so sick that all I  could it was like plain dry what I mean  cooked but like no sauce pasta at least  I was getting a little bit more protein  in that so that was another great option  but bottom line I would say smaller  energy dense meals and ideally ones  without any kind of strong scent or odor  like fishy things were a hard pass for  me next question is it as scary as it  seems from the outside I'm not really  sure if that question was referring to  pregnancy in general or like in  fertility and IVF but let's keep it a  pregnancy and say I mean sure like there  are scary aspects of of pregnancy  especially in that first trimester I  can't tell you how nerve-wracking every  day is like as somebody who's gone  through a lot of infertility and gone  through a lot to actually get here to  get pregnant to get that positive  pregnancy test  yeah like every day especially in 