 for me and I loved it and I am  actually genuinely excited to do it  again alright next question what  prenatal vitamin do you recommend I mean  there's lots of great brands out there  so choose something that's within budget  for you but I do always recommend  something with methyl folate or  methylated folate rather than just  simple Foley which coz methylated fully  is the active form of folate and so I  like rituals prenatal vitamin that  methyl Foley in it and also mega foods  baby and me too that's what I'm using  right now but yeah lots of great brands  out there choose a brand that works for  your budget but also ideally that has  the methylfolate when did you start  taking your prenatal vitamin so I guess  for me I just like didn't really ever  stop you know I remember and I've said  this many times that my my university  professor in nutrition school said you  know if you're a childbearing age you  should be taking a prenatal vitamin  because mistakes can happen and it's  really important to be getting that  extra folate in for those early weeks of  pregnancy often before women even know  that they're pregnant so I was taking it  I know I think it probably started  before I was like married and thinking  about having kids and then I took it all  throughout IVF to get through pregnancy  took through breastfeeding because it's  also can really help with breastfeeding  your your nutritional needs are a lot a  lot higher in breast and breast feeding  than when you're not breastfeeding so  that was important and then I went  through your breast feeding right back  into IVF and preparing for pregnancy and  then into pregnancy so I'm probably just  gonna stay on it for for for I don't  know maybe forever  I don't know depends I know it's a  little bit more expensive than a normal  multivitamin but you never know like  maybe a miracle accident will happen and  I'd rather be safe than sorry  okay have you gained more weight in this  pregnancy than you did in your 