ys  a little unnerving when your clothes  don't fit even if obviously in pregnancy  you're meant to gain weight and I know I  talk all the time about body positivity  but I will say body positivity is not  necessarily looking your body every  single day and thinking that it is like  Rockstar super sexy all the time to me  it's really about respecting your body  and honoring your body's needs which is  something of course I will continue to  do and have been continuing to do  despite the fact that like hey sometimes  I just feel kind of bloated and and and  bigger like there's a long period in  pregnancy where you don't really look  super pregnant you just look bigger your  clothes don't fit but you don't have  that cute  the ball bub that you can show off you  just feel a look not like yourself and  that can be kind of uncomfortable I've  also found that in my second pregnancy  this is very common a lot of my friends  say this but I showed showed a lot  faster and a lot bigger than I did in my  first pregnancy and like everyone has  mentioned that to me like about me  so side note folks never comment on a  woman's body period but even in  pregnancy pregnancy does not give you  the right to comment on or touch a  woman's body without asking you know I'm  joining to do a whole video on this cuz  I I could go off on this so leave me a  comment below if you want to see any  rant on all the things you should never  say or do to a pregnant woman when it  comes to her body I I will go off but  anyways  sometimes hearing these remarks even  though I consider myself a pretty  confident person and I feel quite  comfortable in my own skin and in my own  body even when it is changing if someone  is really hurt to hear that from people  but anytime that I have a negative  thought if I look in the mirror I just  say to myself wow how Abby think about  how amazing your body is for doing  everything that it's doing right now and  I also tell myself you know my body is  so smart it 